{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon3d_diffusion_vertical_robin_surface",
    "description": "MMS driver: variable-coefficient VERTICAL TURBULENT DIFFUSION coupled to a ROBIN SURFACE-EXCHANGE boundary -- dry deposition out, prescribed emission in -- on the 3-D latlon3d grid, u_t = D(kz * D(u,lev), lev) + S, discretized by grids/latlon3d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_lev_robin_surface_bc (zero-flux model top, resistance-in-series ground). This is the operator that couples a chemical transport model to its surface: it carries emitted tracer up out of the bottom layer and delivers depositing tracer back down to it. The sibling of problems/latlon3d_diffusion_vertical_noflux -- identical mesh, identical diffusivity, identical interior and lid -- differing ONLY in the surface boundary condition, so the two convergence goldens isolate exactly what the surface exchange costs (answer: nothing; both are 2.00). PASSIVE lon (NLON = 8) and lat (NLAT = 5). MANUFACTURED SOLUTION u*(z,t) = phi(z) + exp(-pi^2 t) psi(z), a transient decaying onto an emission/deposition STEADY STATE, with phi(z) = 1 - 0.5 sin(pi z/2) and psi(z) = cos(pi z) - 1. The split is what makes a Robin condition with a STATIC emission field admissible at every t: phi carries the inhomogeneous part (it fixes emis = vdep*phi(0) - kz(0) phi'(0)), while psi satisfies the HOMOGENEOUS Robin condition (psi(0) = psi'(0) = 0, so kz(0) psi'(0) = vdep psi(0) trivially); both have zero derivative at z = 1, matching the no-flux lid. Forcing S = u*_t - d/dz(kz du*/dz) splits into a STEADY part -d/dz(kz phi') and a TRANSIENT part exp(-pi^2 t)[-pi^2 psi - d/dz(kz psi')], spelled below as two aggregates over cell centres. WHY THE SURFACE CLOSURE IS NOT THE OBVIOUS ONE. The rule closes the ground flux by RESISTANCE IN SERIES, G_1/2 = (vdep*u[1] - emis) * a/(a + vdep) with a = 2 kz[1]/dz[1], rather than applying the deposition velocity directly to the first-cell value. The naive form is INCONSISTENT -- it commits an O(dz) error in the ground flux, which the divergence divides by dz[1], leaving an O(1) truncation error. Measured on THIS manufactured solution the naive closure looks healthy at coarse resolution and then unravels (Linf order 1.98 -> 1.52 -> 1.16 as NLEV goes 32 -> 64 -> 128); the series form holds 2.00. See grids/latlon3d/stencils/varcoeff_D_lev_robin_k1.esm for the derivation. MASS: the column budget closes to exactly the physical surface exchange -- mass is not conserved here, by design. VERTICAL MESH: as the no-flux sibling (quadratic stretch, thin cells at the ground). HYGIENE: pe over kn, kz over (ik,jk,kk), forcings over (ia,ja,ka)/(ib,jb,kb), vdep over (iv,jv), emis over (ie,je), dz/zc via gk -- all distinct from the operator's (i,j,k). ic/references spell z inline from the stretch formula and the NLEV name (build-time scope caveat).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "op:varcoeff_laplacian",
      "axes:lev",
      "bc:robin",
      "family:finite_volume"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Wesely, M. L., & Hicks, B. B. (2000). A review of the current status of knowledge on dry deposition. Atmospheric Environment, 34(12-14), 2261-2282.",
        "doi": "10.1016/S1352-2310(99)00467-7"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Jacobson, M. Z. (2005). Fundamentals of Atmospheric Modeling (2nd ed.). Cambridge University Press. Section 20.1 (surface emission and dry-deposition flux boundary condition)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. Journal of Fluids Engineering, 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "VerticalDiffusionRobin3d": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_lev_robin_surface_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Emitted / depositing tracer over lon x lat x lev (horizontally uniform here). Cell-centre values on the stretched vertical mesh."
        },
        "pe": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Level-edge coordinates of the quadratic-stretch vertical mesh, pe[kn] = 0.6 s + 0.4 s^2 with s = (kn-1)/NLEV, over node kn = 1..NLEV+1 (pe[1] = 0 at the ground, pe[NLEV+1] = 1 at the model top; monotone increasing since dpe/ds = 0.6 + 0.8 s > 0). Cells are THIN near the surface and thicken upward, which is the physically right stretch for a boundary-layer-resolving column. Identical to the mesh of problems/latlon3d_advection_vertical_ppm, so the advection and diffusion operators are exercised on the same vertical grid. HYGIENE: aggregates over the node index `kn` (not k), so inlined pe[k]/dz[k]/zc[k] reads do not capture a consuming vertical stencil's own aggregate index k.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "kn"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "kn": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.6,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.4,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cell thicknesses dz[k] = pe[k+1] - pe[k], derived by the grid's lev_thickness template (which aggregates over the geometry index gk). This is the `dz` free name read by the diffusion rule's stencils.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lev_thickness",
            "bindings": {
              "pe": "pe"
            }
          }
        },
        "zc": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cell centres zc[k] = (pe[k] + pe[k+1])/2, derived by the grid's lev_center template (aggregating over the geometry index gk). Read here only to build the diffusivity kz and the manufactured forcing; the diffusion stencils themselves need only `dz`.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lev_center",
            "bindings": {
              "pe": "pe"
            }
          }
        },
        "kz": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Vertical turbulent diffusivity Kzz(z) = 0.5 (1 + 4 z (1 - z)), a parabolic boundary-layer mixing profile: it vanishes nowhere on [0,1] (range [0.5, 1.0]), peaks at mid-column and falls to 0.5 at the ground and the lid, which is the classic O'Brien/Troen-Mahrt shape of a well-mixed PBL. Horizontally uniform here (the vertical operator is what is under test), but declared with the full [lon,lat,lev] shape the rule's match requires so a real consumer can supply a genuinely 3-D Kzz. Bound by the rule's match as the coefficient kz -- the LEFT factor of kz * D(u, lev). HYGIENE: aggregates over (ik, jk, kk), all distinct from the operator's (i, j, k).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "ik",
              "jk",
              "kk"
            ],
            "args": [
              "zc"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "ik": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jk": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "kk": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                0.5,
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    1,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        4,
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "zc",
                            "kk"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "zc",
                                "kk"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "vdep": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Dry-deposition velocity at the ground, vdep = 0.3 (uniform here; a real consumer supplies a land-use / stability-dependent field). Read by the rule's surface slab as the `vdep` free name. Enters the ground flux through the resistance-in-series conductance a*vdep/(a+vdep), a = 2 kz[1]/dz[1].",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "iv",
              "jv"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "iv": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jv": {
                "from": "lat"
              }
            },
            "expr": 0.3
          }
        },
        "emis": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Surface emission flux, emis = 0.6926990816987242 (uniform here). NOT a free choice: it is fixed by the manufactured solution, emis = vdep*phi(0) - kz(0) phi'(0) = 0.3 + (pi/4)(0.5), which is exactly the value that makes the steady part phi(z) = 1 - 0.5 sin(pi z/2) satisfy the continuous Robin condition at the ground. Physically: phi decreases upward, so the Fickian flux -kz phi_z is UPWARD out of the ground (an emission plume), and emission exceeds deposition by exactly enough to sustain it. Read by the rule's surface slab as the `emis` free name.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "ie",
              "je"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "ie": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "je": {
                "from": "lat"
              }
            },
            "expr": 0.6926990816987242
          }
        }
      },
