      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_varcoeff_vertical_diffusion_robin_surface_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(z,t) = phi(z) + exp(-pi^2 t) psi(z) for u_t = d/dz(kz du/dz) + S with kz(z) = 0.5(1 + 4z(1-z)), a no-flux lid and a Robin ground (vdep = 0.3, emis = vdep + pi/8). A transient relaxing onto the emission/deposition steady state phi. The t = 0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t = 0.1 assertion bounds the L2 discretization error, which falls at order 2 in both L2 and Linf -- the same order as the no-flux sibling, i.e. the resistance-in-series surface exchange costs nothing in accuracy. Exact per-resolution error values are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/latlon3d_diffusion_vertical_robin_surface/golden/errors.json.",
